1. MAIN-TERM CONVENTION AND SANITY GATES
==============================================================================
Convention ADOPTED: M(r,d) = Delta^(d+1) of R(2^.) at r, R =
Riemann's function (mpmath riemannr). O34's TRUE_RES_R20 literals
are R-stencil residuals -- the gate below shows the R column
matching every literal to its printed precision while the li
column misses depths 0-2 by 23.8 / 5.9 / 1.5 -- and R is the
smooth part of the J-expansion whose oscillating part IS the Ei
mode sum, so li would leave an unmodeled li - R floor no number
of zeros removes. The li-stencil (unoffset; the offset constant
is annihilated by the stencil) is carried as a comparison column
at every headline cell.

(a) d = 0: M(r,0) vs the true block count, both conventions
    r= 15  true=    1612  M_R=   1618.3526687  resid_R=  -6.352669  M_li=   1624.3556614  resid_li=  -12.35566
    r= 20  true=   38635  M_R=   38659.886479  resid_R=  -24.88648  M_li=   38683.716252  resid_li=  -48.71625
    scale check: both residuals are the differenced |pi - smooth|
    gap, O(sqrt(x)/log x); li overestimates pi on this range.

