==============================================================================
5. PSI-FORM CROSS-CHECK - same cells, psi's OWN table
==============================================================================
The psi modes target Delta^(d+1) psi(2^.), not the pi integer;
certifying the pi count with psi modes would need the mu-sum /
1/log conversion O34 never implements. So the cross-check asks
the SAME +-0.5 question of the psi table itself: true values
are exact prime-power sums of log p; main term is
Delta^(d+1)[x - (1/2)log(1-x^-2)] (-log 2pi annihilated by the
stencil; the ln2/2 jump-midpoint offset at x = 2^m likewise).
psi cells are NOT integers, so +-0.5 has no integer meaning
here -- this column is a parallel-behaviour check only.

